decision_inputs.which_governs:
THE HELD-OUT INTERVAL DECIDES. The scale only splits the straddle case:
- held-out Delta MSE excludes 0 on the rules' side -> "better" (shrinking the rules to 0 cannot produce this);
- excludes 0 on the baseline's side -> "worse" (the falsifier);
- straddles 0, AND the training-set scale interval includes 0 -> "calibration removes the rules: no magnitude of the compiled rules improves on no rule" (a negative);
- straddles 0, AND the scale interval excludes 0 -> "inconclusive".
A negative scale is reported beside whichever reading applies, as "the rules point the wrong way on average". Every reading carries the prior-exposure sentence (this RNA was read by items 7, 7d, 7h and today's capped-sum census).
